exports[`heat panels on the real Esch data (characterization) > renders the story panel 1`] = `"Satellite data backs the PRO-SUD heat studyIn 2024, the PRO-SUD communes, LIST and GEO-NET mapped summer heat across Esch and 10 neighbouring communes (Bioklima-Analyse für die PRO-SUD Region). The study named specific hot and cool spots in Esch. Below is what satellites measured at those spots over 4 summers. Read the study (PDF) ↗Spots named in the study · satellite surface temperature, June–August median, 2022–2025Named hotRue Zénon Bernard (dense centre)40.5°CEsch-Schifflange industrial site40.2°CAn der Schmelz car parks39.2°CTown hall square38.9°CBoulevard Kennedy37.0°C0.5°C gap — no overlapNamed coolPark Clair-Chêne*36.5°CParc Laval34.4°CBrucherbierg-Lalléngerbierg edge33.9°C* approximate location+13.1°CHottest public/residential spot, 2025 — Rue de Luxembourg8 of 28Schools & care sites in the hottest 10% — Lycée Guillaume Kroll (3 of 4 summers), Espace Garage Dicks (2 of 4 summers), +6 moreBoulevard Kennedy: a heat hotspot in the PRO-SUD study, and NO₂ still +35% above the 2030 value.Industrial land excluded above: active-plant process heat isn't something commune planning can change.Satellite: surface temperature, ~11:00, 100m, June–August median. PRO-SUD study: modelled air temperature and felt heat on one simulated day. Never blended."`;
